"""Buyer-focused application, materials, service and guide content."""
INDUSTRIES=[
('beauty-skincare','Beauty & skincare packaging','Coordinate cartons, gift boxes, retail bags and printed inserts around bottles, jars and daily routines.','Bottle and jar dimensions, cap clearance, glass protection, variant information and product removal.','Separate everyday retail units from discovery kits and gift sets. A carton may need an insert to control movement; an ecommerce order may need a second protective layer.','Review fragrance or oil contact, cosmetic surface marking and product presentation. Text and variant differences should remain readable on the final print.',['custom-boxes/folding-cartons','custom-boxes/rigid-boxes','paper-bags/luxury-shopping-bags','cards-tags/care-cards','stickers-labels/clear-labels'],'beauty'),
('perfume','Perfume packaging','Build a presentation around bottle geometry, finish and the way a fragrance set is opened.','Bottle weight, cap height, fragile details, fragrance variants and whether the retail box ships alone.','A rigid presentation box and a compact folding carton solve different problems. The insert needs to hold the bottle without creating difficult removal or marking the surface.','Sample with the actual bottle and cap. Review closure feel, insert contact and the outer transit configuration as separate decisions.',['custom-boxes/magnetic-gift-boxes','custom-boxes/lid-and-base-boxes','custom-boxes/box-inserts','paper-bags/paper-gift-bags'],'beauty'),
('coffee-tea','Coffee & tea packaging','Connect coffee pouches, tea cartons, retail bags and labels around your roasting or blending workflow.','Whole bean or ground product, fill weight, freshness target, valve need and sealing equipment.','The shape of a bag does not define its barrier. Compare stand-up, flat-bottom and side-gusset formats using filled samples and an agreed material direction.','Review seal contamination, zipper clearance, valve placement and aroma protection requirements. Match material evidence to the actual construction.',['flexible-pouches/flat-bottom-pouches','flexible-pouches/side-gusset-bags','flexible-pouches/stand-up-pouches','stickers-labels/roll-labels'],'coffee'),
('food-snacks','Food & snack packaging','Choose flexible pouches, cartons and labels around the product, serving format and retail environment.','Product texture, oil content, moisture sensitivity, fill weight, intended shelf life and packing process.','Fragile snacks, fine powders and dense ingredients occupy different volumes at the same weight. A filled trial helps establish the usable size before print is approved.','Food-contact and shelf-life claims require evidence for the selected material and intended use. Review sealing, distribution and applicable labelling with qualified advisers.',['flexible-pouches/stand-up-pouches','flexible-pouches/three-side-seal-pouches','flexible-pouches/printed-rollstock','custom-boxes/window-boxes'],'general'),
('bakery','Bakery packaging','Plan cartons, paper bags and labels for baked products and their handling requirements.','Product dimensions, temperature at packing, grease exposure, fragility and expected time to consumption.','Allow for toppings and presentation without leaving the product uncontrolled. Compare a viewing window, a plain carton and an additional protective tray against actual handling.','Confirm any direct-contact requirements and condensation conditions. A paper appearance alone does not establish grease resistance or food suitability.',['custom-boxes/window-boxes','custom-boxes/folding-cartons','paper-bags/kraft-paper-bags','stickers-labels/paper-labels'],'packing'),
('chocolate','Chocolate packaging','Organise individual chocolates, bars and gift assortments with fitted paper structures and printed details.','Piece size, cavity layout, product contact, temperature exposure and the required gifting experience.','A sleeve can coordinate existing trays; a separate lid-and-base box can organise an assortment. Confirm the food-contact layer independently from the decorative outer pack.','Check surface contact, movement and temperature-related marks. Any protective performance needs verification with the actual product and route.',['custom-boxes/lid-and-base-boxes','custom-boxes/box-inserts','custom-boxes/packaging-sleeves','paper-bags/paper-gift-bags'],'beauty'),
('pet-food','Pet food & treat packaging','Review pouch shape, filling, resealing and handling around dry food and treat products.','Product edges, density, oil content, fill weight, closure needs and the expected storage conditions.','A pouch that fits a dense kibble may not fit a light treat at the same weight. Compare filled dimensions, seals and the secondary-carton layout before choosing artwork proportions.','Review puncture risks, seal contamination and moisture or aroma requirements. Do not assume a bag is suitable because another pet product uses a similar shape.',['flexible-pouches/stand-up-pouches','flexible-pouches/flat-bottom-pouches','flexible-pouches/quad-seal-bags','stickers-labels/roll-labels'],'general'),
('supplements','Supplement packaging','Develop pouches, cartons and information cards around powder, capsule or portion-pack requirements.','Dose format, fill process, moisture sensitivity, container dimensions and the intended market.','Choose the primary contact structure first. Outer cartons and inserts can then organise instructions, variants and product presentation without making unsupported health claims.','Product claims and mandatory wording need the product owner’s approval. Confirm barrier, closure and traceability needs for the actual contents.',['flexible-pouches/stand-up-pouches','flexible-pouches/sachets','custom-boxes/folding-cartons','cards-tags/product-information-cards'],'general'),
('apparel','Apparel packaging','Connect garment bags, shipping mailers, shopping bags, hang tags and care cards in one range.','Folded garment size, delicate surfaces, barcode position, order configuration and sales channel.','A product bag keeps a garment organised; a mailer addresses the delivery route; a shopping bag supports retail carrying. Specify these layers according to their separate jobs.','Review snagging, film contact, ventilation and closure. Check printed care instructions with the product owner before approving tag and card artwork.',['plastic-bags/garment-bags','plastic-bags/poly-mailers','cards-tags/hang-tags','cards-tags/care-cards','paper-bags/luxury-shopping-bags'],'packing'),
('jewellery','Jewellery packaging','Create fitted presentation, product information and gifting layers for compact accessories.','Product profile, delicate finishes, tangling risk, display orientation and closure preference.','An insert should locate the item while allowing easy removal. Compare drawer and lid-and-base formats with the actual jewellery and any protective product bag.','Check contact points and loose small components. Review surface marking and the security of the packed item during handling.',['custom-boxes/drawer-boxes','custom-boxes/lid-and-base-boxes','custom-boxes/box-inserts','cards-tags/care-cards'],'beauty'),
('candles','Candle packaging','Plan cartons, inserts and gift boxes around candle vessels, lids and parcel movement.','Vessel dimensions and weight, lid configuration, surface sensitivity and shipment method.','The retail carton and the outer shipper may need different board and supports. Begin with the complete vessel, not only its labelled diameter.','Check vessel movement, edge contact and printed-surface rubbing. Review temperature and transit conditions separately from decorative presentation.',['custom-boxes/folding-cartons','custom-boxes/box-inserts','custom-boxes/shipping-boxes','stickers-labels/roll-labels'],'beauty'),
('gifting','Gift packaging','Bring boxes, paper bags, cards and seals together around the opening experience.','Contents, arrangement, occasion, handling route and whether the set is assembled before shipping.','Specify the insert and access first, then coordinate colors and decorative details. A recurring gift range may need artwork versions without changing the underlying structure.','Review scuff protection, assembly time and the fully packed presentation. Keep fragile and cosmetic surfaces away from unsuitable direct contact.',['custom-boxes/rigid-boxes','custom-boxes/magnetic-gift-boxes','paper-bags/paper-gift-bags','cards-tags/thank-you-cards','stickers-labels/packaging-seals'],'beauty'),
('ecommerce','Ecommerce & subscription packaging','Build a packing system from a mailer or shipping box, product bags, labels and a clear insert.','Typical order combinations, packed weight, fulfilment workflow, returns and destination.','A subscription set may change contents each month. Test the smallest and largest intended order rather than sampling only an ideal arrangement.','Review closure, movement, packing speed and any return route. Attractive print does not replace transit validation.',['custom-boxes/mailer-boxes','custom-boxes/shipping-boxes','plastic-bags/poly-mailers','cards-tags/insert-cards','stickers-labels/packaging-seals'],'packing'),
('personal-care-refills','Personal care & refill packaging','Compare flexible refill formats and printed supporting packaging around the formulation and filling process.','Viscosity, ingredients, filling temperature, dose or dispensing needs and existing equipment.','A spout format needs compatible film, fitment and sealing details. Match its opening and dispensing behavior to the real product and consumer use.','Carry out formulation compatibility and leak checks. A refill concept does not automatically establish environmental benefit or broad material compatibility.',['flexible-pouches/spout-pouches','flexible-pouches/stand-up-pouches','stickers-labels/clear-labels','cards-tags/product-information-cards'],'beauty'),
('electronics','Electronics packaging','Organise devices, cables and instructions within fitted cartons, inserts and shipping protection.','Device dimensions, accessory set, surface sensitivity, weight and distribution conditions.','Separate cosmetic presentation from functional protection. A paper insert can position components, but specialist protection requirements need their own materials and evidence.','Review movement, cable retention and printed instructions. Do not assume ordinary paper or plastic packaging provides ESD or other specialist protection.',['custom-boxes/box-inserts','custom-boxes/mailer-boxes','custom-boxes/folding-cartons','cards-tags/product-information-cards'],'packing')]

MATERIALS=[
('paperboard','Paperboard packaging','Choose paperboard around carton structure, print and the loaded product.','Paperboard is used for folding cartons, sleeves, cards and tags. Grade, caliper, grain direction, coating and surface condition influence folding and print behavior; a heavier sheet is not automatically the right answer.','Start with the finished dimensions and the load on the base and closure. Review scores, corners, glue and printed coverage on a formed sample. A flat press sheet cannot establish how a dark panel will look after folding.','Ask for the agreed board description, reference sample, color proof and any required source documentation. Keep environmental or contact claims tied to that particular grade and finished construction.',['custom-boxes/folding-cartons','custom-boxes/packaging-sleeves','cards-tags/insert-cards']),
('corrugated-board','Corrugated packaging materials','Match corrugated construction to the packed product and its journey.','Corrugated board combines liners and a fluted medium. Liner finish, flute, construction, dimensions and the way a box is assembled all influence the final pack; flute names do not establish a finished box rating.','Specify product weight, stacking, handling and the complete internal arrangement. Inserts, tape and closure are part of the review, as are the space and equipment used at the packing bench.','Agree the validation method for the actual distribution conditions. Request the relevant board specification and inspect print, fold and closure behavior with a loaded sample.',['custom-boxes/mailer-boxes','custom-boxes/shipping-boxes','custom-boxes/box-inserts']),
('kraft-paper','Kraft paper packaging','Review paper appearance and function as separate decisions.','Kraft paper gives bags, wraps and some packaging surfaces a characteristic visual direction. Natural shade can vary, and printed colors may differ from artwork viewed against a white screen.','Define paper, print coverage, handling and the required package structure. Review light inks, dark solids and fine text on the chosen paper rather than approving from a generic white proof.','Ask about the finished construction and any coating, adhesive or liner. Natural appearance is not evidence that a complete package is recyclable, compostable or suitable for direct food contact.',['paper-bags/kraft-paper-bags','paper-bags/twisted-handle-bags','custom-boxes/packaging-sleeves']),
('barrier-films','Barrier films for flexible packaging','Choose a film direction from the product and packing conditions.','Oxygen, moisture, light, aroma, puncture and seal requirements are separate parts of a flexible-packaging brief. Neither pouch shape nor a metallic appearance gives a complete barrier specification.','Share contents, shelf-life target, temperature, humidity, filling process and distribution. Compare measured properties using matching test methods and conditions; do not compare unrelated numbers as though they describe the same performance.','Confirm the actual material layers and intended use with relevant documents and product trials. Packaging alone cannot establish shelf life without the product and its storage conditions.',['flexible-pouches/stand-up-pouches','flexible-pouches/flat-bottom-pouches','flexible-pouches/printed-rollstock']),
('recyclable-structures','Recyclable packaging structures','Evaluate the complete structure against the destination’s collection and processing route.','Paper, film, labels, closures, coatings, inserts and adhesives can create different end-of-life questions within one package. A mono-material direction may simplify a brief, but does not prove local collection or sorting access.','Compare material reduction, protection and the applicable recovery system together. A pack that loses product or fails in transit creates a different tradeoff from a well-matched package.','Request evidence for the exact claim, material structure and market. Avoid broad labels such as universally recyclable or biodegradable without qualified evidence and any required conditions.',['paper-bags/kraft-paper-bags','custom-boxes/folding-cartons','flexible-pouches/stand-up-pouches']),
('printing-finishes','Packaging printing & finishes','Use print and finishing to support the graphic design and the structure.','Full-color print, spot colors, white ink, foil, embossing and selected coatings produce different visual and tactile effects. Availability depends on material, production route, artwork and quantity.','Define solid areas, small text, color priorities and fold placement. A bright pouch, a coated carton and an uncoated card may need coordinated references rather than one identical ink instruction.','Approve a suitable proof or physical sample. Check registration, foil or coating placement, folds, scuffing and readability on the final material. An illustrative render is a design direction, not print approval.',['custom-boxes/rigid-boxes','flexible-pouches/stand-up-pouches','cards-tags/hang-tags','stickers-labels/roll-labels'])]

SERVICES=[
('structural-design','Packaging structural design','Begin with the contents, the packing operation and the product journey.','Provide products or accurate dimensions, weights, orientation and sales channel. The structural brief identifies what must be held, protected, displayed, opened and removed.','Compare format, internal fit, closure, insert and assembly method. Resolve the physical layout before placing critical text, barcodes or decorative elements on a final dieline.','Use a structural sample to confirm fit and access. Record the approved dimensions and revision so a later artwork change does not silently change the package.',['custom-boxes/box-inserts','custom-boxes/folding-cartons']),
('sampling','Packaging samples & prototyping','Choose a sample according to the decision you need to approve.','A stock sample can help screen size or format. A plain structural sample addresses fit and assembly. Printed samples and production-representative samples address different questions about artwork and materials.','State whether the priority is shape, color, finish, sealing, filled-pack behavior or transit. One sample does not automatically validate every part of the order.','Record sample type, limitations, changes and approval. Confirm which reference and specification are carried into production and how later revisions will be reviewed.',['custom-boxes/mailer-boxes','flexible-pouches/stand-up-pouches']),
('artwork-preflight','Packaging artwork preparation','Prepare artwork that can be checked against the agreed dieline and print route.','Provide the current dieline, final copy, artwork files, color references and intended finishes. Keep cut, fold, glue, seal and non-print zones identifiable to the prepress team.','Check bleed, image resolution, fonts, line detail, small type, white ink and finish layers where applicable. Review critical information at actual size, including barcodes and QR codes.','Approve an identified artwork version and proof. The product owner remains responsible for wording, claims, translations and correct codes; preflight does not establish regulatory approval.',['cards-tags/product-information-cards','stickers-labels/roll-labels']),
('quality-control','Packaging quality-control planning','Agree what will be checked before the production run starts.','Create a specification covering structure, material, artwork version, quantity, features, reference samples and packing. Identify which cosmetic and functional points matter most to the product.','Plan appropriate checks for dimensions, print, finish, seals, assembly or fitted contents. Define methods and acceptance criteria rather than relying on general quality language.','Keep inspection findings tied to the order and specification. Discuss any nonconformity, correction and approval before release; no universal performance rating is implied.',['custom-boxes/shipping-boxes','flexible-pouches/spout-pouches']),
('export-packing','Export packing & shipment planning','Include the outer shipment configuration in the packaging brief.','Provide the destination, expected mode of transport, unloading conditions and delivery window. Distinguish product production timing from freight and customs-related steps.','Review packing quantities, carton dimensions, weight, protection between finished surfaces and pallet direction where applicable. Flat supply and assembled supply may require different shipment plans.','Confirm shipping terms, marks, documents, responsibility and arrival assumptions in the quotation. Prices and delivery dates require project-specific confirmation.',['custom-boxes/shipping-boxes','paper-bags/luxury-shopping-bags']),
('multi-product-sourcing','Multi-product packaging sourcing','Coordinate different packaging components in one clear procurement brief.','List each box, bag, pouch, card and label with its quantity per size and design. Identify common colors, artwork versions, packing relationships and the launch window.','Confirm how the components fit together. A card, seal and outer bag can look coordinated yet fail if their sizes, finishes or adhesive needs were specified separately.','Maintain a component list and approved references. Quote each product line clearly, including responsible supply, samples, commercial terms and the planned delivery sequence.',['custom-boxes/folding-cartons','paper-bags/paper-gift-bags','cards-tags/insert-cards','stickers-labels/packaging-seals'])]

EXTRA_GUIDES=[
('folding-cartons-vs-rigid-boxes','Folding cartons vs rigid boxes: what should you choose?','Compare shipment efficiency, structure and the opening experience.', [('Start with the purpose','Folding cartons are formed from a cut and scored paperboard blank and often travel flat. Rigid boxes use a more defined board structure, commonly wrapped with printed or decorative paper. Each can suit different retail and presentation requirements.'),('Compare fit and packing','Consider product movement, insert needs, assembly and removal. A rigid outer form does not automatically remove the need for a fitted insert, while a well-designed folding carton can organise a compact retail unit efficiently.'),('Compare the complete order','Review dimensions, quantity, finishes, samples, assembly and freight on the same basis. Do not choose from a picture alone: two similar-looking formats may involve different packing labor and shipment volume.'),('What should the sample answer?','Check the intended opening, product clearance and contact surfaces using the real contents. Confirm print and finish separately from structure when the sample route does not represent the final material.')]),
('internal-vs-external-box-dimensions','Internal vs external box dimensions: how should you specify size?','Avoid quoting a box from an ambiguous measurement.', [('Start with usable internal space','Internal dimensions describe the space intended for the contents. External dimensions describe the outside of the finished box and include the construction. The difference depends on board, structure and folds; there is no single allowance for every box.'),('Measure the complete product','Include caps, lids, protective bags and any other parts that remain inside the box. Specify orientation and the clearance needed for packing and removal. Give units with every measurement.'),('Allow for the insert and the closure','A fitted tray can occupy space that appears empty on a flat drawing. Closure flaps and opening access may also affect the usable layout. Record the agreed order of length, width and depth on the dieline.'),('Confirm the assembled sample','Measure and pack the sample, record its revision and confirm which dimensions are controlled in production. Outer shipping or shelf constraints should be specified in addition to product-fit requirements.')]),
('packaging-print-proof','CMYK and Pantone packaging proofs: what should you approve?','Use the right reference for color, material and finishing decisions.', [('Separate screen color from printed color','A screen emits light, while a printed pack reflects it. Substrate, coating, ink coverage and lighting affect appearance. A digital visual is useful for layout but cannot establish every physical color or tactile detail.'),('State the color priorities','Identify brand colors, critical solids, images and any spot-color references. Ask which print route is proposed. A spot-color reference is not a promise that different materials will look identical under every light.'),('Review the finished structure','A carton proof, a flexible film and an uncoated card may need separate approval references. Check white ink, foil, coating, registration and text around folds or seals as applicable.'),('Record the approved reference','Identify the proof type, material, artwork version and viewing conditions. Keep changes visible and agree which reference governs production. If a sample cannot represent a specific effect, clarify that limitation before approval.')]),
('packaging-sample-types','Packaging sample types: what does each one verify?','Choose samples by decision rather than by appearance.', [('Stock samples','Stock samples can help you understand a material direction, general format or approximate fit. Their usefulness depends on how close they are to the intended structure. They do not establish the final artwork or complete specification.'),('Structural samples','Plain or unprinted structures help check dimensions, assembly, product fit and opening. Use the actual product when possible and document the changes to the dieline.'),('Printed samples','A printed sample helps inspect layout and certain print decisions. Confirm whether its material and print route represent the planned order before treating it as a color or finishing standard.'),('Production-representative samples','When risk calls for a sample close to the planned construction, agree what it represents and what remains to be tested. Record filling, sealing, contact or transit checks separately instead of assuming every sample proves them.')]),
('label-roll-direction','Roll label unwind direction: what should you confirm?','Prevent a correctly printed label from arriving on an unusable roll.', [('Start with the applicator','Obtain the labelling-machine specification or the hand-application workflow. The label face, leading edge and direction it leaves the roll must match the equipment and container orientation.'),('Describe the roll','Specify label width and pitch, gap, liner, core and outer diameter. Supplier numbering conventions can differ, so include a diagram showing exactly how the label feeds rather than relying on a number alone.'),('Review print orientation','A portrait label can be printed correctly yet arrive rotated relative to the application path. Mark the top of the artwork, the leading edge and the adhesive side on the approval reference.'),('Run an application trial','Check dispensing, detection, alignment and adhesion on the actual product. Confirm any changes before the complete quantity is produced. Keep the approved unwind drawing with the artwork revision.')]),
('paper-bag-load-testing','Paper bag load testing: what should a buyer review?','Check the complete bag with the product it will carry.', [('Define the intended load','Record the contents, weight, shape and carrying time. A smooth product and an item with sharp corners create different stresses. Paper weight alone does not establish the performance of a finished bag.'),('Include handles and the base','Handle attachment, reinforcement, seams and base folds work together. Load the assembled bag and review how the contents sit, whether handles feel comfortable and where stress concentrates.'),('Match the conditions','Dry indoor carrying, humidity and repeated handling can produce different results. Agree test conditions and acceptance criteria that reflect the intended use instead of relying on an undocumented lifting demonstration.'),('Keep a reference','Identify the tested construction, sample and load. If paper, adhesive, handles or dimensions change, review whether the original result still applies. A sample test should not become an unlimited carrying guarantee.')]),
('brand-color-across-materials','Brand color across packaging materials: how do you coordinate it?','Plan one graphic identity across cartons, pouches, bags and cards.', [('One brand, several substrates','Uncoated paper, coated board, clear film and metallic surfaces reflect light differently. A single artwork color value cannot describe every visual effect across these materials.'),('Choose a hierarchy of references','Identify the most important brand color, acceptable relationships between components and the viewing context. Share physical references where useful and confirm the print route for each product.'),('Account for the structure','Folds, seals, embossing and coatings change the way a design is seen. Place logos and slogans where they remain readable after forming, filling and handling rather than only on a flat layout.'),('Approve a coordinated set','Review representative samples together under agreed conditions. Record each material and artwork version. Coordination means managing the relationships within the range, not claiming every printed surface will be physically identical.')])]
